# NestJS Architecture

## Architectural style

Modular monolith. Business modules under `src/modules/`:

```text
src/modules/example/
├── example.module.ts
├── example.controller.ts
├── example.service.ts
├── dto/
├── example.repository.ts
└── tests/
```

Supporting folders:

- `src/common` — reusable NestJS building blocks.
- `src/config` — typed configuration.
- `src/database` — Drizzle integration.
- `src/integrations` — email and external adapters.
- `src/jobs` — BullMQ jobs.
- `src/health` — health checks.

## Layer responsibilities

### Controllers

- Parse transport input; decorators for auth, validation, Swagger.
- Call one service method; return DTO/presenter.
- No database access or heavy business logic.

### Services

- Use cases and business rules.
- Coordinate repositories, transactions, adapters.
- Throw typed application exceptions.

### Repositories

- Encapsulate Drizzle queries; explicit types.
- Support transaction client parameter.
- Authorization remains in services/guards.

### DTOs

- Transport-specific; validate every field.
- Reject unknown properties via global ValidationPipe.
- Never include server-controlled fields.

Never expose password hashes, refresh-token hashes, or reset token hashes.

## Dependency rules

- Business modules depend on shared infrastructure through exported providers.
- Avoid circular module dependencies; do not default to `forwardRef()`.
- External SDKs behind interfaces in `src/integrations` when practical.

## Naming

- Files: kebab-case.
- Classes: PascalCase.
- Methods/variables: camelCase.
- Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE.

## Error handling

- Typed errors mapped centrally.
- No SQL/stack leakage to clients.
- Map constraint failures to stable API codes when appropriate.

## Transactions

Use for multi-step state changes: token consumption + user update, session rotation races, etc. Keep callbacks small; no slow external calls inside transactions.

## Configuration

- Validate env at startup.
- Typed config service; avoid scattered `process.env`.
- Fail fast on missing required values.
- `.env.example` placeholders only.

## Bootstrap expectations

- Global prefix `/api`.
- ValidationPipe: whitelist, forbidNonWhitelisted, transform.
- Helmet, CORS allowlist, exception filter, rate limiting where applicable.
- Swagger per environment policy.
